+					 * away asks for 1008 MHz, and 1008 MHz is the row
+					 * of the vendor OPP table that reads 960 mV.
+					 *
+					 * ⚠ THIS PATCH AND THE 1008 MHz PIN ARE ONE
+					 * CHANGE. Split them and one half is a hazard:
+					 * this rail alone at 960 mV is merely wasteful,
+					 * but the clock alone at 1008 MHz runs the GPU
+					 * UNDER its voltage curve, which is the failure
+					 * mode that does not announce itself.
+					 *
+					 * Order is right by construction: the regulator
+					 * core writes this at PMIC probe, and the GPU's
+					 * rate is applied when powervr probes, seconds
+					 * later. Voltage up first, then clock.
+					 *
+					 * min == max on purpose. This is a FIXED
+					 * operating point, not a ladder: there is no OPP
+					 * table and no devfreq, and drm/powervr reads no
+					 * regulator at all (grepped in the tree we build:
+					 * zero hits for "regulator" and "-supply" under
+					 * drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/). A wider window
+					 * would therefore never be narrowed by anyone --
+					 * a window is enforcement, not a wish.
+					 *
+					 * Silicon, read on the 6 GiB board (i2cget -f -y 1 0x36):
+					 *   0x15 = 0x9e -> DVM on, n=30 -> 800 mV
+					 *   0x1b = 0x00 -> poly-phase bits [6]/[7] clear,
+					 *                  so DCDC4+5 are NOT paralleled
+					 *                  and this rail is the GPU's
+					 *                  alone. First measured
+					 *                  2026-07-22, re-read 2026-09-08.
+					 * Windows: schematic rates VDD-GPU 0.8-0.96 V and
+					 * DS Tab. 5-1 gives -0.3..1.2 V absolute, so 960
+					 * mV is the top of the design window and stays
+					 * 240 mV under the limit.
+					 *
+					 * ⚠ 960 mV itself is NOT derived from any
+					 * document. No datasheet carries an OPP table for
+					 * this SoC (freq<->voltage comes
+					 * from DT/eFuse and is bin-dependent), and the two
+					 * device trees that do carry one disagree with
+					 * each other everywhere except this pair. It is
+					 * the vendor's number, adopted because it is the
+					 * conservative end of the disagreement and inside
+					 * the documented window -- and it is owed a
+					 * measurement, which a GL render test can give:
+					 * that test fails on wrong PIXELS before the GPU
